<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
  <section xml:id="section-debugging">
    <title>Code debugging activity</title>
      <title>Code debugging activity</title>
      <p>Every week, a new cat or dog was featured as the Ann Arbor’s 107one Pet-of-the-Week in 2020. The code below is supposed to <em>get the pet of the week webpage from September of 2020, scrape the text of the title shown in the picture, and print it</em>.</p>
      <figure xml:id="fig-pet">
        <caption>The pet of the week from August 22, 2020 was Chester.</caption>
        <image source="bsoup/pet_of_the_week.png" width="70%"/>
      </figure>
      <p>However, it doesn't work! Instead of printing the text of the <c>a</c> tag, it prints nothing.</p>
      <p>Can you fix it? Try to fix the buggy code below. Run the code to save your progress.</p>
      <activity label="debug_code_1" xml:id="debug_code_1">
        <statement>
          <p>Fix the code below:</p>
          <program label="debug_code_1-editor" interactive="activecode" language="python3">
            <code>
# Get the webpage
#  Load libraries for web scraping
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup
import requests

# Get a soup from a URL (using the Wayback Machine)
url = ''https://web.archive.org/web/20200927230337/https://www.hshv.org/petsoftheweek/''
r = requests.get(url)
soup = BeautifulSoup(r.content, 'html.parser')

# Get info from one tag
#  Get first tag of a certain type from the soup
tag = soup.find('a', class_='pt-cv-none cvplbd')

# Get info from tag
info = tag.get('href')

# Do something with the info
#  Print the info
print(info)
            </code>
          </program>
        </statement>
      </activity>
    </section>